WEBVTT

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:09.185
♪

00:00:13.015 --> 00:00:15.670
[ sighs]

00:00:19.848 --> 00:00:23.287
♪

00:00:26.768 --> 00:00:29.902
HERMIONE [ whispers]:
Harry?

00:00:29.945 --> 00:00:32.034
I saw my dad.

00:00:32.078 --> 00:00:33.427
[ gasping]:
What?

00:00:33.471 --> 00:00:35.560
He sent the
dementors away.

00:00:35.603 --> 00:00:37.170
I saw him
across the lake.

00:00:37.213 --> 00:00:39.303
Listen, Harry,
they've captured Sirius.

00:00:39.346 --> 00:00:40.478
Any minute,
the dementors

00:00:40.521 --> 00:00:42.088
are going to perform
the kiss.

00:00:42.131 --> 00:00:43.829
You mean they're
gonna kill him?!

00:00:43.872 --> 00:00:46.440
No, it's worse.
Much worse.

00:00:46.484 --> 00:00:49.878
They're going
to suck out his soul.

00:00:51.053 --> 00:00:52.925
Headmaster, you've
got to stop them!

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:54.187
They've got
the wrong man!

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:55.841
It's true, sir.
Sirius is innocent!

00:00:55.884 --> 00:00:57.843
RON:
It's Scabbers
who did it.

00:00:57.886 --> 00:00:58.887
Scabbers?

00:00:58.931 --> 00:01:00.411
He's my rat, sir.

00:01:00.454 --> 00:01:02.108
He's not really a rat.

00:01:02.151 --> 00:01:04.284
Uh, well, he was rat.
He was my brother Percy's rat.

00:01:04.328 --> 00:01:05.938
But then they gave him
an owl, then I got...

00:01:05.981 --> 00:01:08.375
Point is, we
know the truth.

00:01:08.419 --> 00:01:09.811
Please believe us.

00:01:09.855 --> 00:01:11.247
I do, Miss Granger.

00:01:11.291 --> 00:01:12.597
But I'm sorry to say,

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.208
the word of three
13-year-old wizards

00:01:15.251 --> 00:01:17.906
will convince
few others.

00:01:19.081 --> 00:01:22.520
A child's voice,
however honest and true,

00:01:22.563 --> 00:01:23.869
is meaningless...

00:01:23.912 --> 00:01:25.044
[ gasps, whimpers]

00:01:25.087 --> 00:01:26.219
...to those
who have forgotten

00:01:26.262 --> 00:01:28.177
how to listen.[ sniffs]

00:01:31.442 --> 00:01:35.141
Mysterious thing, time.

00:01:35.184 --> 00:01:36.534
Powerful.

00:01:36.577 --> 00:01:40.712
And when meddled with...
dangerous.

00:01:40.755 --> 00:01:42.235
Sirius Black is in

00:01:42.278 --> 00:01:45.194
the topmost cell
of the Dark Tower.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.762
You know the laws,
Miss Granger.

00:01:47.806 --> 00:01:49.242
You must not be seen.

00:01:49.285 --> 00:01:51.462
And you would do well, I feel,

00:01:51.505 --> 00:01:53.942
to return
before this last chime.

00:01:53.986 --> 00:01:55.553
If not,
the consequences

00:01:55.596 --> 00:01:57.642
are too ghastly
to discuss.

00:01:57.685 --> 00:01:59.165
If you succeed
tonight,

00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:02.908
more than one innocent life
may be spared.

00:02:02.951 --> 00:02:04.213
[ distant tolling]

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:08.000
Three turns
should do it, I think.

00:02:11.307 --> 00:02:13.571
Oh, by the way...

00:02:13.614 --> 00:02:15.311
when in doubt,

00:02:15.355 --> 00:02:19.403
I find retracing my steps
to be a wise place to begin.

00:02:19.446 --> 00:02:21.405
Good luck.

00:02:21.666 --> 00:02:24.712
What the bloody hell
was that all about?

00:02:24.756 --> 00:02:28.803
Sorry, Ron, but seeing
as you can't walk...

00:02:30.588 --> 00:02:34.330
[ steady chiming]

00:02:37.464 --> 00:02:41.425
[ chiming, clock ticking]

00:02:45.124 --> 00:02:49.389
[ distorted conversations
playing in reverse]

00:02:57.092 --> 00:02:58.398
What just happened?

00:02:58.442 --> 00:02:59.617
Where's Ron?

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:00.966
7:30.

00:03:01.009 --> 00:03:02.620
Where were we
at 7:30?

00:03:02.663 --> 00:03:04.622
I don't know.
Going to Hagrid's?

00:03:04.665 --> 00:03:06.885
Come on!
And we can't be seen!

00:03:06.928 --> 00:03:08.495
[ pants]

00:03:08.539 --> 00:03:10.889
Hermione!

00:03:13.021 --> 00:03:16.503
[ creaking]

00:03:16.547 --> 00:03:19.158
[ tolling]

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:27.732
[ squawking]

00:03:27.775 --> 00:03:29.516
HARRY:
Hermione!

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.561
Hermione, wait!

00:03:30.604 --> 00:03:32.650
Hermione,
will you please

00:03:32.693 --> 00:03:34.652
tell me what it is
we're doing?

00:03:34.695 --> 00:03:35.696
DRACO:Ah!

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:36.784
Come to see
the show?

00:03:36.828 --> 00:03:38.090
HERMIONE:
You! You foul,

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:39.526
loathsome, evil
little cockroach!

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.223
But... that's us.

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:42.834
RON:
Hermione, no!

00:03:42.877 --> 00:03:44.531
He's not worth it.

00:03:44.575 --> 00:03:46.707
This is not normal.

00:03:47.229 --> 00:03:49.144
This is a
Time-Turner, Harry.

00:03:49.188 --> 00:03:51.843
McGonagall gave it
to me first term.

00:03:51.886 --> 00:03:54.019
This is how
I've been getting

00:03:54.062 --> 00:03:55.716
to my lessons
all year.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:58.502
You mean, we've gone
back in time?

00:03:58.545 --> 00:04:00.068
Yes.

00:04:00.112 --> 00:04:04.116
Dumbledore obviously wanted
us to return to this moment.

00:04:04.943 --> 00:04:09.687
Clearly something happened
he wants us to change.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.037
DRACO [ grunts]:
Oh!

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:13.560
Good punch.Thanks.

00:04:13.604 --> 00:04:14.561
GOYLE:Malfoy?

00:04:14.605 --> 00:04:15.562
Are you okay?
Come on!

00:04:15.606 --> 00:04:16.694
Let's go!
Come!

00:04:16.737 --> 00:04:17.651
Malfoy's coming!

00:04:17.695 --> 00:04:18.652
Run!Wait for me!

00:04:18.696 --> 00:04:20.219
Not a word
to anyone.

00:04:20.262 --> 00:04:21.568
Understood?Okay!

00:04:21.612 --> 00:04:23.657
I'm gonna get that
jumped up mudblood!

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:24.963
You mark my words!

00:04:25.006 --> 00:04:26.355
HERMIONE:
That felt good.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:27.748
RON:
Not good--

00:04:27.792 --> 00:04:29.358
brilliant!

00:04:29.924 --> 00:04:30.751
HARRY:Come on.

00:04:30.795 --> 00:04:32.797
We should be
at Hagrid's.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.583
[ clock ticking]

00:04:51.772 --> 00:04:52.686
Look.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:55.515
Buckbeak's
still alive.

00:04:55.559 --> 00:04:56.603
Of course.

00:04:56.647 --> 00:04:59.693
Remember
what Dumbledore said?

00:04:59.737 --> 00:05:01.216
If we succeed,

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.610
more than one innocent
life could be spared.

00:05:03.654 --> 00:05:06.439
[ whispers]:
Let's go!

00:05:15.796 --> 00:05:19.626
[ Hagrid speaking]

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.194
HAGRID:
Great man, Dumbledore!

00:05:22.237 --> 00:05:23.630
Great man.

00:05:23.674 --> 00:05:24.936
[ birds cawing]

00:05:24.979 --> 00:05:26.807
FUDGE:
Up there. Right up at the...

00:05:26.851 --> 00:05:28.026
HARRY:
Here they come.

00:05:28.069 --> 00:05:29.636
I'd better hurry.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.465
Fudge has to see Buckbeak
before we steal him.

00:05:32.508 --> 00:05:35.207
Otherwise, he'll think
Hagrid set him free.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:36.643
RON:
Scabbers! He's alive!

00:05:36.687 --> 00:05:39.472
HAGRID:
Keep a closer eye
on your pets.

00:05:39.515 --> 00:05:40.821
That's Pettigrew.

00:05:40.865 --> 00:05:42.257
Harry, you can't!

00:05:42.301 --> 00:05:43.650
Hermione, that's the man
who betrayed my parents.

00:05:43.694 --> 00:05:45.652
You don't expect me
to just sit here.

00:05:45.696 --> 00:05:48.481
Yes, and you must!

00:05:49.917 --> 00:05:52.050
Harry, you're in
Hagrid's hut now.

00:05:52.093 --> 00:05:55.836
If you just go bursting in,
he'll think you've gone mad.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:59.927
Awful things happen to wizards
who meddle with time, Harry.

00:05:59.971 --> 00:06:01.146
We can't be seen.

00:06:01.189 --> 00:06:02.669
DUMBLEDORE:
Do you remember

00:06:02.713 --> 00:06:05.367
this foot path, Minister,
from your school days here?

00:06:05.411 --> 00:06:06.542
Fudge is coming.

00:06:06.586 --> 00:06:07.979
And we aren't leaving?

00:06:08.022 --> 00:06:10.068
HERMIONE:
I think that means

00:06:10.111 --> 00:06:11.809
you owe someone
an apology.

00:06:11.852 --> 00:06:13.593
Why aren't we leaving?

00:06:13.637 --> 00:06:15.464
RON:
Next time I see
Crookshanks...

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:16.988
HERMIONE:
I meant me.

00:06:17.031 --> 00:06:19.251
FUDGE:
There are many
changes, I think,

00:06:19.294 --> 00:06:21.601
looking 'round, you know.

00:06:21.645 --> 00:06:23.734
[ grunts]

00:06:23.777 --> 00:06:25.039
[ gasps]

00:06:25.083 --> 00:06:26.388
Blimey! What was that?Are you mad?

00:06:26.432 --> 00:06:27.825
DUMBLEDORE:
Yes, he was a good man.

00:06:27.868 --> 00:06:29.174
I wasn't fond of him...

00:06:29.217 --> 00:06:30.523
Ow!

00:06:30.566 --> 00:06:32.351
Ow. That hurt....did all the planting here.

00:06:32.394 --> 00:06:33.482
All that planted
vegetation,

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.049
variegated leaves, flowers.Sorry.

00:06:35.093 --> 00:06:36.703
Oh, variegated?
Called what?

00:06:36.747 --> 00:06:38.444
DUMBLEDORE:
Oh, I have no idea,

00:06:38.487 --> 00:06:39.837
but it's very fine stuff.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.708
But I can find the name.Uh-huh.

00:06:41.752 --> 00:06:42.709
Here, uh, here we are.

00:06:42.753 --> 00:06:44.189
[ knocking on door]

00:06:44.232 --> 00:06:46.539
DUMBLEDORE:
Yes, yes. That's ling.

00:06:46.582 --> 00:06:47.758
The ling, see over there?

00:06:47.801 --> 00:06:49.542
That's all...On the slope? Yes.

00:06:49.585 --> 00:06:50.717
On the slopes, all ling.

00:06:50.761 --> 00:06:51.936
Ah, Hagrid. How are you?

00:06:51.979 --> 00:06:53.502
HAGRID:
Professor Dumbledore. Minister.

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:55.374
Just, uh,
just make your way through.

00:06:55.417 --> 00:06:56.723
FUDGE:
Good evening, Hagrid.

00:06:56.767 --> 00:06:59.683
We're coming
out the back door. Go.

00:07:05.645 --> 00:07:08.779
FUDGE:
It is the decision
of the Committee

00:07:08.822 --> 00:07:12.217
for the Disposal of Dangerous
Creatures that the hippogriff

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:14.785
known as Buckbeak, hereinafter
called "the condemned..."

00:07:14.828 --> 00:07:17.831
Is that really what my hair
looks like from the back?

00:07:17.875 --> 00:07:19.180
Hermione![ branch snaps]

00:07:19.224 --> 00:07:22.053
HARRY:
What?

00:07:22.096 --> 00:07:25.186
HERMIONE:
I thought I just saw...

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:26.405
Never mind.

00:07:26.448 --> 00:07:27.580
RON:
Let's go!

00:07:27.623 --> 00:07:29.190
FUDGE:
The Executioner

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:33.934
shall dispatch the condemned
by means of beheading.

00:07:33.978 --> 00:07:36.589
As witness here
under Hagrid,

00:07:36.632 --> 00:07:37.851
please sign here.
Just here.

00:07:37.895 --> 00:07:39.766
DUMBLEDORE:
I-I really think the Minister

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:43.074
might feel it in his heart
to have a change of mind.

00:07:43.117 --> 00:07:44.466
Okay, go, Harry. Go!

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:47.165
FUDGE:
It is the decision
of the Committee,

00:07:47.208 --> 00:07:48.383
Professor Dumbledore.

00:07:48.427 --> 00:07:49.776
Nothing you or I
can do will change it.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.647
[ birds cawing]Off!

00:07:51.691 --> 00:07:52.953
Get away! Get off!

00:07:52.997 --> 00:07:54.781
DUMBLEDORE:
Minister,

00:07:54.825 --> 00:07:56.261
you really want to be...

00:07:56.304 --> 00:07:58.089
[ hippogriff grunts]the hippogriff?

00:07:58.132 --> 00:07:59.090
FUDGE:
No, I do not.

00:07:59.133 --> 00:08:00.439
DUMBLEDORE:
Very well, then.

00:08:00.482 --> 00:08:04.225
FUDGE:
I saw him just the other day.

00:08:04.269 --> 00:08:06.358
The Executioner
is acting

00:08:06.401 --> 00:08:08.926
on behalf
of the Committee.

00:08:08.969 --> 00:08:10.057
[ caws]
Ow!

00:08:10.101 --> 00:08:11.102
[ grunts]

00:08:11.145 --> 00:08:13.321
FUDGE:
Very well, gentlemen.

00:08:13.365 --> 00:08:14.801
Shall we step outside?

00:08:14.845 --> 00:08:16.107
DUMBLEDORE:
Uh, Minister?

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:18.544
I-I really think I
should sign as well.

00:08:18.587 --> 00:08:20.024
FUDGE:
Yes, very well.

00:08:20.067 --> 00:08:21.460
Well, perhaps it would be

00:08:21.503 --> 00:08:22.722
a good thing
if you were to.

00:08:22.766 --> 00:08:24.115
[ whispers]:
Okay, Buckbeak?

00:08:24.158 --> 00:08:25.203
Come on, quickly.

00:08:25.246 --> 00:08:26.813
Come with us now, okay?
Come on.

00:08:26.857 --> 00:08:28.510
FUDGE:
I should be very happy
if you'd like to keep it.

00:08:28.554 --> 00:08:30.121
And would you...
would you care to sign?

00:08:30.164 --> 00:08:32.993
[ whispers]:
Keep trying.

00:08:33.037 --> 00:08:34.821
Come on. Beaky!

00:08:34.865 --> 00:08:36.170
[ gurgled grunting]

00:08:36.214 --> 00:08:37.215
Buckbeak.

00:08:37.258 --> 00:08:38.433
Okay, quickly. Hurry up, okay?

00:08:38.477 --> 00:08:39.652
FUDGE:
No, not that spot.

00:08:39.695 --> 00:08:40.827
Just here
on the line.

00:08:40.871 --> 00:08:42.220
Your name only.

00:08:42.263 --> 00:08:43.961
DUMBLEDORE:
It's a very long
name, Minister.

00:08:44.004 --> 00:08:46.137
Hurry up now, Buckbeak, okay?

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:48.661
[ gurgled grunting]

00:08:48.704 --> 00:08:50.315
Come on. Come on, Buckbeak.

00:08:50.358 --> 00:08:51.620
[ grunts]

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:53.274
Come and get the
nice dead ferret.

00:08:53.318 --> 00:08:55.102
[ squawks]

